  "ingredients": [
    "1 large onion",
    "0.35 ounce bird's eye chile pepper",
    "2 tablespoon coconut oil",
    "3 tablespoon low-carb ketchup",
    "1/2 teaspoon salt (or to taste)",
    "2 drop liquid sucralose"
  ],
  "instructions": [
    {
      "text": "Roughly chop the onion and blend in a blender until smooth. Set aside.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-sambal/#wprm-recipe-51615-step-0-0",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/homemade-sambal-step-01.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "To prepare chili paste, roughly cut the dried chilis and remove seeds. Boil them for about 30 minutes or until soft.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-sambal/#wprm-recipe-51615-step-0-1",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/homemade-sambal-step-02.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Once soft and cooled, blend to a paste.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-sambal/#wprm-recipe-51615-step-0-2",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/homemade-sambal-step-03.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "In a pan over medium heat, melt the coconut oil. Once it becomes hot add in the blended onion, chilies, reduced sugar ketchup, and salt. Let simmer for a few minutes until the oil separates from the sauce.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-sambal/#wprm-recipe-51615-step-0-3",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/homemade-sambal-step-04.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Use this sambal as a sauce or a cooking seasoning in future recipes! This sauce is featured in the Ketogenic Nasi Lemak recipe.",
      "group": "",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.ruled.me/homemade-sambal/#wprm-recipe-51615-step-0-4",
      "imageSource": "https://www.ruled.me/wp-content/uploads/2015/03/homemade-sambal-step-05.jpg"
    }
